<h2>Sources and further reading</h2>
<p>The key and placement drawings are conceptual models. Native observations come from a disposable Linux CockroachDB v26.2.8 single-node fixture with a two-CPU limit, a 1,536 MiB container limit, 256 MiB SQL memory and 64 MiB cache. They establish the recorded SQL paths and controlled lock wait, not distributed survival, regional timing or workload acceptance. Indexes were declared before loading; online build behaviour was not measured. Primary documentation checked 26 October 2026.</p>
<ul>
<li>CockroachDB v26.2: <a href="https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/v26.2/explain-analyze">EXPLAIN ANALYZE</a> and <a href="https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/v26.2/explain">EXPLAIN</a>, for native plan fields and execution modes.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/v26.2/indexes">Secondary indexes</a> and <a href="https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/v26.2/joins">Joins</a>, for covering, stored columns and lookup work.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/v26.2/hash-sharded-indexes">Hash-sharded indexes</a>, including v26.2’s <code>shard_columns</code> prefix selection, and <a href="https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/v26.2/create-index">CREATE INDEX</a> for clause ordering.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/v26.2/understand-hotspots">Understand hotspots</a>, <a href="https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/v26.2/show-ranges">SHOW RANGES</a> and <a href="https://www.cockroachlabs.com/docs/v26.2/load-based-splitting">Load-based splitting</a>, for relating demand to key bounds and owners.</li>
